ogether then pack into a  jar top it up with a bit more of the  brine then leave the ferment for several  days making sure to submerge the top  every day until it tastes sour and  begins to bubble  this homemade lemonade will get you  through the hottest summer days all  right try to find some of the leaves on  they're so fragrant peel the zest of 5  lemons and juice the fruits to get  around 300 milliliters slightly break a  handful of leaves to release the aroma  then slice around 40 grams of ginger 100  grams cane sugar 750 milliliters water  add the lemon peels along with the  leaves and the ginger slowly bring to a  boil then turn off the heat and leave to  infuse for 30 minutes drain the liquid  and add the lemon juice then fill it  into a bottle  and keep in the fridge  let's make an indian breakfast curry all  right  one tablespoon of tea a quarter teaspoon  coriander seeds 10 dried perry leaves  until toasted one garlic clove and a  quarter teaspoon of chili powder a  quarter teaspoon turmeric and half a  teaspoon garam masala  then add 2 large tomatoes 1 small  aubergine and half a teaspoon salt  a 10 grams chopped coriander 100  milliliters of water and the eggs cook  for five minutes until thickened  have you ever sliced something without  feeling fully in control over the blade  you've got to change the way you hold  your knife this is my number one tip  that helped me improve my knife skills  alright instead of just holding the  handle use your thumb and index finger  to grip the blade then rest the blade  against your knuckles as a guide and  start slicing this way the knife becomes  an extension of the hand and you have  much more control over how you slice  lots of you couldn't believe that it  would work with anything else but a soft  avocado but it does it works with pretty  much everything like cucumbers carrots  apples onions and even potatoes  oh yes  [Music]  you
 

